.TH WIFI-ANALYZER 1 "2026-10-30" "WiFi Analyzer 0.1.36" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wifi-analyzer \- inspect nearby Wi-Fi networks and channel use
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wifi-analyzer
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wifi-analyzer
uses NetworkManager to list nearby access points. It shows signal strength,
frequency, channel, security, channel overlap and local regulatory hints.
Channel recommendations exclude frequencies outside ranges reported by the local
regulatory domain when that information is available.
When multiple Wi-Fi devices are available, it prefers the device with an active
NetworkManager connection and reads active-link details from that interface.
.PP
The application keeps scan history locally. Exporting a scan always requires
choosing a destination file.
.SH WI-FI GENERATIONS
For an active connection, WiFi Analyzer can identify HT, VHT, HE and EHT PHY
markers reported by
.BR iw (8),
and presents them as Wi-Fi 4, 5, 6/6E and 7. A scan result for an unconnected
access point does not reliably identify its Wi-Fi generation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/wifi-analyzer/history.json
Private local scan history.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR iw (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Daniel Nylander.
